[[0,623937,0,10,0,10,"2015-10-29T21:42:17","ChillyHellion","",[],"","Mirrors Edge Catalyst has been delayed into May 2016","http://www.vg247.com/2015/10/29/mirrors-edge-catalyst-has-been-delayed-into-may-2016/","gaming"],[1,3010455,0,3,0,3,"2015-10-29T22:33:11","poopbutt","",[],"<p>Good, I'd rather have them take their time and polish up the game than EA forcing them to shit it out unfinished just to meet arbitrary financial quarter schedules or anything like that.</p>"],[2,3010484,3010455,0,0,0,"2015-10-29T22:35:21","ChillyHellion","",[],"<p>I've definitely warmed up to that perspective in the past year of releases. </p>"],[1,3010500,0,2,0,2,"2015-10-29T22:37:11","torky","",[],"<p>Games being delayed left and right. Publishers should really start listening to developers. Delays disappoint fans and diminishes the hype, increasing the chance that a fan won't buy the game. </p>"],[2,3025818,3010500,0,0,0,"2015-10-31T04:44:51","Datawych","",[],"<p>It's because most developers are god awful at estimating how long it'll take them to do something, and without good evidence, marketing always wins.</p>"],[1,3013983,0,1,0,1,"2015-10-30T04:20:56","baphometsrage","",[],"<p>Good, it'll give me time to actually play the first one, which I bought back during the summer sale haha.</p>"]]
